From 43c864621ea3c098b5129339b2dc2a2f88f15d44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 21:01:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reskin the vertical slice to a space-station theme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Content-only reskin of the existing engine (scrolling 2x2 overworld with
row streaming and in-place text/menu/dialogue boxes over the map). No
engine logic, no docs touched — changes go through the documented content
entry points only:

- tools/gen_assets.py: rethemed terrain art (metal deck, walkway plates,
  bulkhead walls, supply crates, floor vents/lights, a glowing energy
  hazard in the "water" slot), an astronaut hero, a service-droid NPC, a
  one-eyed alien enemy, and space-themed message text. Symbol names
  (MSG_*, frag_*) are unchanged so main.s still resolves them.
- src/main.s: pal_field / pal_battle recolored (steel-gray deck, cyan
  hazard, teal droid, white text; black space void + green alien in
  battle). The recolor is the only main.s change.
- src/chr.s, src/messages.s: regenerated from gen_assets.py.

Map layout, tile ordering, and collision are unchanged, so src/field.s
and src/tiles.inc are byte-identical.

Verified headless end to end: boot, scrolling (hero centered, world pans),
in-place command menu and two-page dialogue over the scrolling map with no
flash, clean map restore on close, encounter, and the alien battle loop
returning to the field at the prior position.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017WhrMENKrWYz9jN2gu1sQQ
---
